  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WINGS-Skills-Building Program for Elected Women Representatives (EWRs) representing 12 Local Councils in the Plantation areas in Nuwara Eliya District</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The total population of the Nuwara Eliya District is approximately 780,000. Of this, 417,136 individuals belong to the plantation sector.  This project seeks to build the leadership and governance capacities of approximately 60 EWRs representing 12 local councils in the plantation areas of the Nuwara Eliya District. With the introduction of the 25% quota, women&#x2019;s representation in local politics increased to a considerable level. However, due to changes in the national level political landscape, a significant number of the women who held office during 2018-2023 did not continue their political career. There is a new cohort of women, introduced by political parties to represent the contestant  and proportional lists. There is a new cohort of women, introduced by political parties to represent the contestant and proportional lists. With the WINGS project, it is expected to build the skills and capacities of women councilors representing the plantation sector of Nuwara Eliya.</narrative>
  </description>
